          "filename": "Long Beach 1933 Earthquake.jpg",
          "caption": "The Long Beach earthquake, estimated magnitude 6.25 Ms, occurred at 5:55 p.m., March 10, 1933. \n\nBrick buildings with unreinforced masonry walls, including many school buildings failed catastrophically.\n120 people died in the quake in Los Angeles County, largely from collapsed buildings or falling debris.\n\"My mother, pictured in the foreground, sustained little or no structural damage.\"",
          "alt": "The Long Beach earthquake, estimated magnitude 6.25 Ms, occurred at 5:55 p.m., March 10, 1933. \n\nBrick buildings with unreinforced masonry walls, including many school buildings failed catastrophically.\n120 people died in the quake in Los Angeles County, largely from collapsed buildings or falling debris.\n\"My mother, pictured in the foreground, sustained little or no structural damage.\"",
